56 506.30 moveto (1. The source problem and its context) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 486.50 moveto (Jeffries and Yeats study a degree-preserving variant of delta-wye transformations, motivated in) show
56 473.20 moveto (part by graphs and Feynman periods. We use the journal version of [1], Definition 2.1 and) show
56 459.90 moveto (Conjecture 5.1, with the arXiv version retained for comparison. The journal distinguishes two) show
56 446.60 moveto (notions: a minimal graph has the least vertex count in its equivalence class; a minimum graph) show
56 433.30 moveto (additionally has the least number of connections among minimal graphs. The conjecture first takes) show
56 420.00 moveto (a smallest pure-reduction result, which we call a pure minimum. This does not assert either) show
56 406.70 moveto (equivalence-class minimality or connection minimality.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 386.90 moveto (Conjecture 5.1 \(verbatim, journal p. 678; typography normalized\):) show
/Times-Italic findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 367.10 moveto (Given a doubled 3-regular graph G, perform the YY-Delta transformation on all wyes in all possible) show
56 353.80 moveto (ways to find a graph G' of the smallest size. Then G' is a minimal graph if and only if it does) show
56 340.50 moveto (not contain a chain of one or more 3-cycles, each connected by a vertex, which is also doubly) show
56 327.20 moveto (adjacent to one more vertex, where the 3-cycles on either end of the chain have one vertex with) show
56 313.90 moveto (exactly 4 neighbours and no connections of size greater than 2.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 294.10 moveto (The surrounding remarks are essential. The source allows the depicted vertices to coincide but) show
56 280.80 moveto (requires distinct edges. It says other Figure 14 gadgets already certify nonminimality of) show
56 267.50 moveto (arbitrary graphs using an expansion first. The conjectured extra assertion concerns pure minima) show
56 254.20 moveto (from doubled cubic inputs. Its examples support a heuristic, not a proved classification. Our) show
56 240.90 moveto (example violates exactly that extra assertion.) show
/Helvetica findfont 8 scalefont setfont
