56 731.00 moveto (2. Moves and the illustrated chain predicate) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 705.50 moveto (All graphs here are finite undirected loopless multigraphs. A symmetric nonnegative integer matrix) show
56 692.20 moveto (A with zero diagonal records edge multiplicities; the degree is its row sum. A connection is the) show
56 678.90 moveto (entire nonempty set of edges between a pair of vertices. Doubly adjacent means that the ambient) show
56 665.60 moveto (connection has size exactly two. A doubled graph replaces each edge of a simple graph by two) show
56 652.30 moveto (parallel edges.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 632.50 moveto (Definition 2.1 removes a degree-six centre x with exactly three distinct neighbours u, v, w, each) show
56 619.20 moveto (joined to x by two edges. It deletes x and its incident edges, and adds one edge on each of uv,) show
56 605.90 moveto (uw, vw. This is YY-Delta \(reduction\). Its inverse, Delta-YY \(expansion\), selects distinct u, v, w) show
56 592.60 moveto (with a positive entry on each triangle pair, subtracts one on those pairs, and adds a new centre) show
56 579.30 moveto (doubly joined to each. Existing parallel edges on the triangle pairs are allowed. Each move) show
56 566.00 moveto (preserves degree six. Equivalence means a finite sequence of either kind, including the empty) show
56 552.70 moveto (sequence; pure reachability uses reductions only.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 532.90 moveto (For precision, the chain predicate follows the verbal description together with Figure 14\(a\), \(b\),) show
56 519.60 moveto (\(d\). Take distinct base vertices b[0],...,b[t] for a positive number t of triangles. Triangle i) show
56 506.30 moveto (uses b[i], b[i+1], and an apex a[i]. Each end base has two double attachments; each internal base) show
56 493.00 moveto (has one double attachment. End bases have four actual neighbours and no ambient connection larger) show
56 479.70 moveto (than two. Every base has degree six. Apex and attachment vertices may coincide with one another or) show
56 466.40 moveto (other vertices whenever the edges can remain distinct.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 446.60 moveto (For every unordered pair, count all schematic edge occurrences, with a double attachment) show
56 433.30 moveto (contributing two. Require that count to be at most the actual multiplicity A[u,v]. This capacity) show
56 420.00 moveto (condition is precisely the availability of distinct parallel-edge copies in each pair's finite) show
56 406.70 moveto (edge pool. It forbids loops automatically. The bases must be distinct: otherwise their disjoint) show
56 393.40 moveto (six incident edge ends would exceed a degree-six vertex's capacity \(and adjacent identified bases) show
56 380.10 moveto (demand a loop\).) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 360.30 moveto (A subtlety matters. A depicted internal double attachment reserves two edges, but under allowed) show
56 347.00 moveto (vertex coincidences it can lie in an ambient triple connection, sharing the pair with a separate) show
56 333.70 moveto (triangle edge. Imposing exact ambient double adjacency on every schematic attachment would exclude) show
56 320.40 moveto (the review's required positive alias control. Likewise, imposing internal row type [1,1,1,1,2]) show
56 307.10 moveto (would be too restrictive. This paper uses the illustrated capacity reading fixed in the ruling and) show
56 293.80 moveto (independently reviewed with that explicit qualification.) show
/Times-Roman findfont 10.7 scalefont setfont
56 274.00 moveto (The earlier discovery lane used a restricted incidence diagnostic and incorrectly said no chain) show
56 260.70 moveto (could leave an endpoint. That diagnostic is not our chain proof. The argument below allows first) show
56 247.40 moveto (triangles through a triple connection and blocks them by residual capacities. The formal statement) show
56 234.10 moveto (uses this same capacity predicate directly; no separate formal equivalence theorem to an edge-ID) show
56 220.80 moveto (embedding API is claimed.) show
